10 is the max).\n    *   Can the Receiver improve? **Yes**. If the Server stays at \"Aim Left,\" the Receiver would prefer to switch from \"Anticipate Left\" (2) to \"Anticipate Right\" (8).\n    *   *Not an equilibrium.*\n\n2.  **(Aim Left, Anticipate Right) — Payoff (4, 8):**\n    *   Can the Receiver improve? No (8 is the max).\n    *   Can the Server improve? **Yes**. If the Receiver stays at \"Anticipate Right,\" the Server would prefer to switch from \"Aim Left\" (4) to \"Aim Right\" (10).\n    *   *Not an equilibrium.*\n\n3.  **(Aim Right, Anticipate Right) — Payoff (10, 2):**\n    *   Can the Server improve? No (10 is the max).\n    *   Can the Receiver improve? **Yes**. If the Server stays at \"Aim Right,\" the Receiver would prefer to switch from \"Anticipate Right\" (2) to \"Anticipate Left\" (6).\n    *   *Not an equilibrium.*\n\n4.  **(Aim Right, Anticipate Left) — Payoff (6, 6):**\n    *   Can the Receiver improve? No (6 is the max for the current state).\n    *   Can the Server improve? **Yes**. If the Receiver stays at \"Anticipate Left,\" the Server would prefer to switch from \"Aim Right\" (6) to \"Aim Left\" (10).\n    *   *Not an equilibrium.*\n\nSince every cell results in at least one player wanting to unilaterally deviate to increase their points, there is no pure-strategy Nash equilibrium.","reasoning":null,"score":1,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"matches no","pattern":"\\b[Nn][Oo]\\b"}]},"breakdown":{"passed":["matches no"],"failed":[],"errored":[]},"timing":{"wall_sec":5.019,"prompt_tokens":176,"generation_tokens":546}},{"item_id":"econ_mixed_server_prob_left","prompt_name":"econ_mixed_server_prob_left","family":"econ-mixed","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"0.5","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"equals 0.4","pattern":"(?<![\\d.])0?\\.40*(?!\\d)"}],"nearMisses":[{"slip":"percent-for-decimal","credit":0.5,"pattern"